; `height` is the PANEL's height, not the opening's -- the opening is
; `opening_h`. This read 5.0 for both, in a chamber whose walls are 10, so
; everything from the doorway's header to the ceiling was nothing at all: a
; 5 x 5 hole straight out of the room, which photographed as an untextured black
; slab hanging over the door in every b_01 and b_02 ever taken. It was diagnosed
; twice as the BossDoor's leaves failing to render and it was never the door --
; the leaves are correct, and were, and are two metres BELOW the black.
;
; The opening is spelled out too. It defaulted to K.DOOR_W x K.DOOR_H (2.4 x 3.2)
; while the BossDoor standing in it is 5.4 x 4.6, so the shut leaves were wider
; than the hole they filled.
